<div class=mywhitetext>

<h3>Service Roles<o:p></o:p></h3>

<p>Service roles are jobs that members provide as a service to other members of
the guild. These jobs can be a large time commitment for the members providing
them. It is asked that you work with the member providing the service and
organize a time to meet that is convenient to both. Demanding access to their
services &quot;right now&quot; is not tolerated. The services they provide take
a lot of time and effort, and should be respected as such.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Note that if the service costs money (i.e. jewelry, alchemy, etc), the
service provider will charge at least the cost of materials, or more than cost
of materials if their skill is lacking to help with their advancement. The
price for the service is up to the member providing the service.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Guild Jeweler</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Responsible for providing jeweler services to Bloodhorde members and
outfitting 47+ members with needed resist jewelry for dragon raids.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Guild Treasurer</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Responsible for having a &quot;mule&quot; character that will maintain the
guild treasury and keep records of donations and withdrawals.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Guild Librarian</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Responsible for having a &quot;mule&quot; character to hold various spell
research components (pages, words, runes, etc) <o:p></o:p></p>

